00:13:02,857 --> 00:13:08,857
Equus is a drama, mystery, thriller film directed by Sidney Lumet.

3
00:19:34,285 --> 00:19:40,285
A psychiatrist, Martin Dysart, investigates the savage blinding of six
horses with a metal spike in a stable in Hampshire, England.

4
00:26:05,714 --> 00:26:11,714
The atrocity was committed by an unassuming seventeen-year-old stable boy named Alan Strang, the
only son of an opinionated but inwardly-timid father and a genteel, religious mother.

5
00:32:37,142 --> 00:32:43,142
As Dysart exposes the truths behind the boy's demons, he
finds himself face-to-face with his own.

6
00:39:08,571 --> 00:39:14,571
Martin Dysart, played by Richard Burton.

7
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:46,000
Alan Strang, played by Peter Firth.

8
00:52:11,428 --> 00:52:17,428
Dora Strang, played by Joan Plowright.

9
00:58:42,857 --> 00:58:48,857
Harry Dalton, played by Harry Andrews.

10
01:05:14,285 --> 01:05:20,285
Frank Strang, played by Colin Blakely.

11
01:11:45,714 --> 01:11:51,714
Hesther Saloman, played by Eileen Atkins.

12
01:18:17,142 --> 01:18:23,142
Equus is a 1977 psychological drama film directed by Sidney Lumet and written
by Peter Shaffer, based on his 1973 play of the same name.

13
01:24:48,571 --> 01:24:54,571
The film stars Richard Burton, Peter Firth, Colin Blakely, Joan Plowright,
Harry Andrews, Eileen Atkins, Kate Reid and Jenny Agutter.

14
01:31:20,000 --> 01:31:26,000
The story concerns a psychiatrist treating a teenager who has blinded horses
in a stable, attempting to find the root of his horse worship.

15
01:37:51,428 --> 01:37:57,428
Lumet's adaptation of the acclaimed play to film incorporated realism through the use of real horses
rather than human actors and provided a graphic depiction of the blinding incident.

16
01:44:22,857 --> 01:44:28,857
Despite some criticism regarding this approach, the film was
praised for the performances of its cast.

17
01:50:54,285 --> 01:51:00,285
The film was nominated for three Academy Awards, including Best
Actor for Burton and Best Supporting Actor for Firth.

18
01:57:25,714 --> 01:57:31,714
The two both won Golden Globe Awards for their performances.

19
02:03:57,142 --> 02:04:03,142
The film was also nominated for four BAFTA Awards, with Jenny
Agutter winning for Best Supporting Actress.

20
02:10:28,571 --> 02:10:34,571
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
